 Heart disease is a big health problem for people and animals all over the world. Many kinds of heart disease exist, but one common type is called cardiomyopathy. This disease happens to humans and many mammals, including dogs. In a type called dilated cardiomyopathy, the heart changes shape and its electrical signals change too. Because of these changes, the heart cannot pump blood well. This means that oxygen and food do not get to the body at the right levels. It can make everyday life hard and can cause early death. Learning about cardiomyopathy and finding the gene changes that cause it is very important. This knowledge helps doctors diagnose, treat, and stop this heart problem. We can try to fix hearts that are broken. In dogs with cardiomyopathy, scientists found gene changes that are linked to heart problems.

