 Just having good ideas is not enough to create a political party. A party needs structure and people to work together.

In American politics, there are two main parts of a party.

The first part is the set of ideas or goals the party says it supports. These ideas can come from real experiences, from what people think is right, or from leaders who want to change things.

The second part is the organization – a group of people who work for the party and help it win elections. Some people join the party because they love its ideas. Others join because they want a job or influence inside the party.

In short, when we talk about a party in the United States, we mean three things:

1. The platform or principles the party says it follows.
2. The voters who believe in those principles.
3. The political workers and leaders who run the party’s organization.

