At that time Harold Grayfell was king of Norway. He was the son of Eric Bloodaxe, who himself was the son of Harold Fair‑hair. Harold’s mother was Gunnhillda, a daughter of Auzur Toti, and the family’s home was east of the King’s Crag. Word soon spread that a ship had arrived in the eastern bay. When Gunnhillda heard the news, she asked about the Icelandic men who were traveling abroad. The men told her that a man named Hrut was Auzur’s brother’s son. Gunnhillda replied, “I see clearly that he intends to claim his inheritance, but there is a man named Soti who has already taken it.”

She then summoned her attendant, Augmund, and said, “I want you to go to the bay, find Auzur and Hrut, and ask them to stay with me this winter. Tell them also that I will be their friend. If Hrut follows my advice, I will help him in whatever he undertakes, and I will speak well of him to the king.”

